# Hobbitify Rule

## Architecture
- Treat this as a multi-app repo:
  - `react-app/` is the primary frontend (React + TS + Tailwind + Vite).
  - `backend/` is Flask-related support.

## Change targeting
- Default to changing `react-app/`.
- If old legacy-frontend references appear, treat them as deprecated unless user explicitly asks for migration work.

## Data and API behavior
- Keep robust parsing for backend responses (string JSON or object).
- Preserve tree semantics:
  - detect root nodes by parent/child relations
  - avoid breaking unlock/progression logic
- Prefer request body shape `{ input: string }` for modern API utilities.

## Code style
- Use existing TypeScript types from `src/types/` and helpers from `src/utils/` before adding new abstractions.
- Keep components readable: extract helper functions when rendering logic becomes dense.
- Follow existing Tailwind design tokens (`bg-*`, `text-*`, `accent-*`, `border-*`) for visual consistency.

## Validation
- After meaningful `react-app/` edits, run `npm run lint`.
- Run `npm run build` when changes affect routing, types, or shared utilities.
